Based on github.com/coder/websocket v1.8.15, retaining its MIT license.

Campfire adds prepared.go and prepared_test.go. PreparedMessage shares immutable
payloads and lazily compressed bytes across server connections negotiating
permessage-deflate without context takeover. WritePrepared writes one or more
prepared messages; when nothing is buffered, their frame headers and payloads go
out in one vectored write (net.Buffers) instead of through the hijacked 4 KiB
writer. It takes the same frame lock and follows the same close-state, timeout
and error handling as writeFrame, and falls back to writeFrame otherwise. Other
connection modes use Write. No upstream Go source files were changed. Upstream
tests run in bin/check.
